            "id": "9d8aef937bc4",
            "text": "The GUI starts `bin\\monitor.exe` automatically, and the monitor stops when the GUI closes. If the monitor is missing or keeps crashing, the status bar shows a warning instead of \"Capturing\".",
            "html": "Version:0.9\r\nStartHTML:0000000105\r\nEndHTML:0000000669\r\nStartFragment:0000000141\r\nEndFragment:0000000633\r\n<html>\r\n<body>\r\n<!--StartFragment--><div style=\"color: #bbbebf;background-color: #121314;font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace;font-weight: normal;font-size: 14px;line-height: 19px;white-space: pre;\"><div><span style=\"color: #bbbebf;\">The GUI starts </span><span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">`bin\\monitor.exe`</span><span style=\"color: #bbbebf;\"> automatically, and the monitor stops when the GUI closes. If the monitor is missing or keeps crashing, the status bar shows a warning instead of \"Capturing\".</span></div></div><!--EndFragment-->\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
